            <div xml:id="d471">

                <pb facs="0448" n="383" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg383"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.711/30: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Merriam</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-04T18:00:00-05:00">November 4, 1936—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. Department’s instruction 266, October 6.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d471-f1"/> In
                    view of the interest of American publishers in delivery of second-class matter
                    in Iran please report by telegraph any important developments which may come to
                    your attention. No direct action by the Legation would apparently be required,
                    however, pending the receipt from the Iranian Postal Administration of reply to
                    recent inquiry of Post Office Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
